## Exports from `src/studio/assistant/exportTools.ts`

- `exportFormats` = `["dxf", "ifc", "drawing-pdf", "material-pdf", "sheet-register"] as const`; `type ExportFormat`.
- `exportDesignSchema` (strict Zod): `{ expectedJobId: id, expectedRevision: int > 0, format: enum(exportFormats), sheetId?: id }` with a superRefine that rejects `sheetId` unless `format === "drawing-pdf"`. `type ExportDesignInput`.
- `exportDesign(sources: ExportSources, input: unknown, deps?: ExportDeliveryDeps): Promise<ExportReceipt>`
  - `ExportSources = { project?: ArchitectProject | null; job?: SheetRegisterJob | null; storage?: Pick<Storage,"getItem"> | null }` where `SheetRegisterJob = Pick<FencingJob, "id" | "revision" | "documents" | "activeDocumentId">`.
  - `ExportDeliveryDeps = { download?(name, bytes: Uint8Array, mimeType): void | Promise<void>; digest?(bytes): Promise<string> }` (digest defaults to `sha256Hex`).
  - Design formats bind `project.id === expectedJobId` and `project.revision === expectedRevision` (design revision). `sheet-register` binds `job.id` and `job.revision` (project record revision) and uses the exact identity logic of `describeSourceSheets` (`sheetSourceIdentity` -> null on sample / missing sha256 or pageCount -> throws; `readSheetLifecycle` from `storage`; `exportSheetRegister`).
  - Receipt: `{ projectId, expectedRevision, format, fileName, mimeType, bytes, byteLength, sha256, deterministic, downloaded, savedToDiskVerified: false, readbackVerified: false, scope, ...detail }`. `scope` is `EXPORT_SCOPE` = "File offered by the browser download; nothing was uploaded or sent anywhere." when `deps.download` ran, otherwise a "no download handler" note with `downloaded: false`. Per-format detail: dxf `{levels, units}`; ifc `{schema}`; drawing-pdf `{sheetId, sheetName, sheetNumber, paper, scale, viewports, pageCount: 1}`; material-pdf `{pageCount, quantityRows, importedAsEvidence: false, materialRegisterSynced: false}`; sheet-register `{documentId, sourceName, sourceSha256, pageCount, lifecycleRevision, sheets, archived}`.
- `describeExportReceipt(receipt)` -> receipt without `bytes` (use this for `text(...)` in appTools).
- `browserDownload(name, bytes, mimeType)` -> calls `saveDownload(bytes, name, mimeType)` from `../architect/sheets.ts` (identical Blob + anchor path the Sketch buttons use); throws "Downloading an export requires a browser." without a DOM.
- `sha256Hex(bytes)` -> lowercase hex over exactly the passed view.
- `EXPORT_SCOPE` constant.

## Suggested appTools.ts wiring (EDIT-class tool: it triggers a browser download, though it never mutates project state)

```ts
import { describeExportReceipt, exportDesign, exportDesignSchema, browserDownload } from "./exportTools.ts";
tool("export_design_file",
  "Download one design export exactly as the Sketch/Sheets export buttons do: dxf, ifc, drawing-pdf (active or chosen authored sheet), material-pdf (download only; not imported as evidence or synced) or sheet-register (active verified source). Requires the current design revision (project revision for sheet-register). Returns sha256 and byte length of the exact bytes handed to the browser download; no file path or on-disk readback is available.",
  objectSchema({ ...bound, format: { enum: ["dxf", "ifc", "drawing-pdf", "material-pdf", "sheet-register"] }, sheetId: id }, ["expectedJobId", "expectedRevision", "format"]),
  async input => {
    const args = exportDesignSchema.parse(input), state = await port.getState();
    if (args.format === "sheet-register") {
      checkProject(state, args.expectedJobId, args.expectedRevision);
      if (!port.storage) throw Error("Sheet organisation storage is unavailable in this session.");
      const receipt = await exportDesign({ job: state.job, storage: port.storage }, args, { download: port.download ?? browserDownload });
      checkProject(await port.getState(), args.expectedJobId, args.expectedRevision);
      return text(describeExportReceipt(receipt));
    }
    checkProject(state, args.expectedJobId);
    const read = await port.architect("read", { expectedJobId: args.expectedJobId }) as { project: ArchitectProject; ready: boolean; blocked: boolean; error: string | null; pendingDraft?: boolean };
    if (!read.ready || read.blocked || read.error) throw Error(read.error || "Architectural design recovery must finish before exporting.");
    if (read.pendingDraft) throw Error("Finish or discard the pending draft before exporting.");
    const receipt = await exportDesign({ project: read.project }, args, { download: port.download ?? browserDownload });
    checkProject(await port.getState(), args.expectedJobId);
    return text(describeExportReceipt(receipt));
  });
```

Port addition (optional, for headless/MCP callers): `download?(name: string, bytes: Uint8Array, mimeType: string): void | Promise<void>` on `AppToolPort`; the browser port can leave it undefined so `browserDownload` is used. Classify as EDIT in skills.ts allow-lists (side effect: a download). Add `src/studio/assistant/exportTools.test.ts` to the `test` script list in package.json.
